cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset or pipeline, please cite it as below, and credit The Columbus Dispatch as the original source of the payroll data."
title: "Olentangy School District Employee Salaries (2025)"
abstract: >-
  Gross pay for 4,238 employees of Olentangy Local School District (Delaware and
  Franklin Counties, Ohio) for calendar year 2025, published as an analysis-ready
  dataset alongside the Dagster pipeline that produces it. The district's published
  position field packs multiple jobs into one delimited string; this dataset splits
  it into a role-level table and extracts contracted days per year, while leaving
  pay figures exactly as published. Employee names are removed. Derived from The
  Columbus Dispatch's central Ohio public payroll database.
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Schieber
    given-names: Rob
    alias: robschieber
license: CC-BY-4.0
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.22849876"
    description: "Concept DOI — always resolves to the latest release"
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.22849877"
    description: "Version DOI for release v2025.3"
keywords:
  - education
  - government
  - employment
  - public sector
  - ohio
  - salaries
date-released: "2026-09-19"

# The upstream compilation this dataset derives from. Credit belongs here: the
# payroll figures are Ohio public record, but the records request and the database
# are the Dispatch's work.
references:
  - type: database
    title: "Public payroll: how central Ohio government agencies spend your money"
    abstract: >-
      Searchable database of payrolls for public, taxpayer-funded agencies across
      the greater Columbus area, obtained through public records requests.
    authors:
      - name: "The Columbus Dispatch"
    url: "https://www.dispatch.com/story/news/local/2026/06/29/public-payroll-how-central-ohio-government-agencies-spend-your-money/90691984007/"
    year: 2026
    notes: >-
      The Dispatch notes that pay classified as "other" can include holiday or
      vacation time, accrued time, and miscellaneous pay or stipends, and that AI
      tools were used to help organize and clean the source database.
